onditional on funding, currency, launch and regulatory execution.\"","\"CALL25\"","\"DECK26\"","null","\"No reliable cohort or legal-entity incremental operating-capital bridge after acquisition and valuation changes. The reconciled broad proxy is reported but insufficient for attribution.\"","\"Low\"","\"3\"","\"FY24–FY26 aggregate group CFO ₹26.49 crore / PAT ₹108.87 crore = 24.33%. Large receivables and inventory cause persistent weak conversion despite parent improvement.\"","\"High\"","\"Large financial assets versus modest borrowings, but investments are not free cash; demand debt, FX, entity transfer and historical guarantee risks remain.\"","\"TAPE\"","\"Revenue execution is strong. B2C 14–15% trails the May 2025 management ambition of 25–30% and the 18–20% target recalled by May 2026 questioners. Registration cohorts are unverified and the clinical unit is pre-revenue.\"","\"Owner earnings grow, but forfeitures and OCI need stripping. EPS uses total PAT including NCI and subsidiary allocations conflict.\"","\"Cash forecasts are not current verified balances; legal-entity minority and free-cash claims remain unresolved. Conditional scenario returns are not underwritable expected returns.\"","\"model assumptions\"","\"Cash-breach scenarios cannot have ordinary drawdown valuations. Realisability and entity claims remain unresolved.\"","\"Observed owner multiples are corrected, but cash-funded intrinsic value and ownership/asset realisation are not sufficiently reliable for a price-versus-value score.\"","\"MASTER\"","\"7\"","\"Framework starting score 9 at 1.971 theoretical days, explicitly reduced to 7 for 100-share lots, top-five-session concentration of 41.85% and the lower 20-session median. Median 5% capacity is two whole lots; unknown spreads/circuits are not adverse facts.\"","\"BQS\"","\"GQS\"","\"IAS\"","\"known_weighted_sum\"","\"coverage\"","\"missing_factors\"","\"numeric\"","\"lower\"","\"upper\"","\"cap\"","\"final\"","\"post_cap_lower\"","\"post